                <pb facs="0572" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/1199: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-18T15:00:00-02:00">February 18, 1933—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 18—12:32 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. Department’s 35, February 17, 5 p.m. Brazilian Government will be pleased to
                    afford Major Sackville every opportunity for observation on Amazon and Putumayo
                    Rivers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
